nflation, so none can reach any rung.\n- **The NDAA votes don't count as records here.** The only report of her votes is her own press release, with no roll call. Final passage of an NDAA is also `multi-subject` under the annex, so the vote couldn't seat a chair even with the roll call.\n- **The $900.6 billion figure isn't her position.** It appears in the release's third-person text, not in her quoted words. It is also never compared with inflation, so it can't separate rung 2 from rung 3.\n- **I put the blank reason as `no-evidence`, not `direction-only`.** Backing an NDAA doesn't even show which side she is on, more spending or less, so no passage separates the sides. This is a judgment call, and it's the field most likely to differ from the other coders.\n- **`needs_source`:** her own words sizing the defense topline, and House roll calls on any amendments that add or cut a stated sum from the defense topline, with the amendment text.\n- **Quotes:** I coded two of her statements as tier `none` and not quotable (`not-forward`, `non-differentiating-goal`).","ttft_ms":9173,"type":"result","duration_ms":28647,"uuid":"49d55f50-e633-4eb2-ae90-61a4a354fe23","ttft_stream_ms":1206,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":1206,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
